# SPI flash layout (the "partition map"). The one place the free numbers live;
# firmware/hal/fm1_flash_map.h derives everything else from them and
# tools/build/flashmap.py gives the package builder and the linker step the same values.
#
# The layout is chosen as a group: FM-1 (the shipped hardware map) or Emulator
# (an 8 MiB chip with a large application area and the FM-1's stores above it;
# fm1-live runs it with --flash-size, its boot stub and loader read these values).
# The two numbers are prompt-less, so no defconfig sets them.

choice FLASH_MAP
    prompt "Flash layout"
    default FLASH_MAP_EMU if EMU
    default FLASH_MAP_FM1
    help
      Which flash map the app, the boot stub, the update loader and the package
      builder use. A package built with the Emulator map does not install on
      an FM-1.

config FLASH_MAP_FM1
    bool "FM-1 (hardware)"
    help
      The layout of the shipped firmware: application area [0x4000, 0x93000),
      body at most 0x8C000 bytes.

config FLASH_MAP_EMU
    bool "Emulator"
    help
      An 8 MiB chip with an application area [0x4000, 0x600000), body at most
      0x5F9000 bytes, for builds that run in fm1-live only. The stores above the
      area are the FM-1's, at their full sizes, shifted up.

endchoice

config FLASH_CHIP_SIZE
    hex
    default 0x800000 if FLASH_MAP_EMU
    default 0x100000
    help
      Size of the flash chip. The FM-1's part is 1 MiB; fm1-live takes any size
      from 1 MiB to 16 MiB (--flash-size, added by the test fixtures and the
      screenshot tool from this value).

config FLASH_APP_END
    hex
    default 0x600000 if FLASH_MAP_EMU
    default 0x93000
    help
      End of the application area [0x4000, FLASH_APP_END). The body (boot stub
      excluded) ends two sectors below it, at the commit-marker sector. Every
      store above it (see hal/fm1_flash_map.h) keeps its size and order and
      follows this value.
